# Eng standup

Thursday, October 8, 2026 at 08:31 · 7 min

## Attendees

- Shreyas
- Maya Chen
- Diego Alvarez
- Priya Nair
- Tom Becker

## Notes

#### Decisions

- The Fernhollow duplicate-jobs incident is closed after two days with zero new duplicates since the fix shipped on Tuesday.
- The read-only offline job list will ship in next week's release, not in today's release cut.
- The flaky webhook retry integration test is quarantined so it does not gate merges or the release cut.
- The release cut happens today (Thursday 8 October) at four o'clock; anything that needs to be in must be merged by three thirty.
- The Outlook time-zone ticket is taken offline to a separate call between Maya and Tom right after standup.

#### Key facts

- **When did the Fernhollow dedupe fix go out?** On Tuesday (6 October 2026); there have been zero new duplicates in the two days since.
- **What is Diego blocked on?** A last modified at field on each job in the jobs list endpoint, which Maya owns, so the mobile app knows when its cached offline copy is stale.
- **How often has the flaky CI test been failing?** About one in eight runs this week, always on the timeout assertion of the webhook retry integration test.
- **What does Priya think causes the flaky test?** The test sleeps for a fixed two seconds before checking the retry fired, and CI runners are slower some days; she wants to confirm before saying for sure.
- **When is the release cut and what is the merge deadline?** Thursday 8 October at four o'clock; merge anything that needs to be in by three thirty.
- **How many items are on Kestrel Audit's evidence request list?** About sixty; Priya has mapped roughly two thirds to evidence Deino already collects.
- **How many support tickets were closed yesterday?** Fourteen, nine of which were Fernhollow cleanup confirmations.
- **What is the new Outlook ticket about?** One technician at a smaller plumbing account sees his jobs an hour off in Outlook; he is in a different time zone from his dispatcher.

## Action items

- [x] Add a last modified at field to each job in the jobs list endpoint for Diego's offline cache — Maya Chen, due Oct 9, 2026
